Branch protection rules Rulesets Rules applying to a branch one rule per branch all matching rulesets, combined with branch protection rules Conflicting settings not applicable the most restrictive version of each rule applies Targets branches branches and tags, pushes for private and internal repositories Scope repository repository, organization or enterprise Default branch matched by name or pattern <code>~DEFAULT_BRANCH</code> follows the default branch Exceptions administrators exempted unless <code>is_admin_enforced</code>, allowances per setting bypass list of roles, teams, users or apps, always or for pull requests only Visibility repository settings anyone with read access can view active rulesets Temporary deactivation remove the rule enforcement <code>disabled</code>, or <code>evaluate</code> to only report violations Merge queue in otterdog not supported <code>required_merge_queue</code> <p>See About rulesets and About protected branches for a complete description.</p> <p>Rulesets can protect the same branch several times, e.g. an organization ruleset defines a common baseline and a repository ruleset adds the checks of the repository:</p> <pre><code>orgs.newOrg('my-project', 'my-org') {
  settings+: {
    plan: "enterprise", // (1)!
  },
  rulesets+: [
    orgs.newOrgRuleset('baseline') {
      include_repo_names+: [
        "~ALL",
      ],
      include_refs+: [
        "~DEFAULT_BRANCH",
      ],
      required_pull_request: null, // (2)!
      required_status_checks: null,
    },
  ],
  _repositories+:: [
    orgs.newRepo('my-repo') {
      rulesets: [
        orgs.newRepoRuleset('default-branch') {
          include_refs+: [
            "~DEFAULT_BRANCH",
          ],
          required_pull_request+: {
            required_approving_review_count: 1,
          },
          required_status_checks+: {
            status_checks+: [
              "build",
            ],
          },
        },
      ],
    },
  ],
}
</code></pre> <ol> <li>Read-only property that reflects the billing plan of the organization. Otterdog currently only accepts    organization rulesets for organizations on the <code>enterprise</code> plan.</li> <li>The baseline blocks force pushes and deletions of the default branch in all repositories.</li> </ol> <p> Open in the Playground</p>
